## 6. Database (PostgreSQL)

### Table: users
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | SERIAL PK | |
| username | VARCHAR(50) UNIQUE | |
| email | VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE | |
| password_hash | VARCHAR(255) | bcrypt hashed |
| role | VARCHAR(20) | Default: 'admin' |
| refresh_token | TEXT | Rotating refresh token storage |
| created_at / updated_at | TIMESTAMP | |

### Table: projects
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | SERIAL PK | |
| title | VARCHAR(100) | |
| description | TEXT | |
| technologies | TEXT[] | PostgreSQL array |
| github_url | VARCHAR(255) | Nullable |
| live_url | VARCHAR(255) | Nullable |
| image_url | VARCHAR(255) | Nullable |
| created_at / updated_at | TIMESTAMP | |

### Table: blog_posts
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | SERIAL PK | |
| title | VARCHAR(200) | |
| content | TEXT | |
| excerpt | VARCHAR(300) | |
| tags | TEXT[] | PostgreSQL array |
| published | BOOLEAN | Default: FALSE (draft) |
| created_at / updated_at | TIMESTAMP | |

### Table: contacts
| Column | Type | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| id | SERIAL PK | |
| name | VARCHAR(100) | |
| email | VARCHAR(100) | |
| message | TEXT | |
| read | BOOLEAN | Default: FALSE |
| created_at | TIMESTAMP | |

### Indexes
- idx_projects_created_at on projects(created_at)
- idx_blog_posts_published on blog_posts(published)
- idx_blog_posts_created_at on blog_posts(created_at)
- idx_contacts_created_at on contacts(created_at)
- idx_users_email on users(email)

### Local Dev Database
Run via Docker:
  docker-compose up -d
  PostgreSQL on port 5432
  DB: portfolio_db | User: portfolio_user | Pass: portfolio_password

---

## 7. Auth Flow

POST /api/auth/login { email, password }
  → Lookup user by email in DB
  → bcrypt.compare(password, hash)
  → Sign accessToken (15m) with JWT_SECRET
  → Sign refreshToken (7d) with JWT_REFRESH_SECRET
  → Store refreshToken in users.refresh_token column
  → Return { accessToken, refreshToken, user }

GET /api/auth/me (Authorization: Bearer {accessToken})
  → jwt.verify(token, JWT_SECRET)
  → Lookup user in DB
  → Return { id, username, email, role }

POST /api/auth/refresh { refreshToken }
  → Lookup user by refresh_token in DB
  → jwt.verify(refreshToken, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET)
  → Issue new accessToken + refreshToken
  → Rotate refresh_token in DB
  → Return { accessToken, refreshToken }

POST /api/auth/logout (Authorization: Bearer {accessToken})
  → Clear refresh_token in DB for this user

---

## 8. Contact Form Flow

1. User fills name, email, message and submits
2. Frontend POSTs to https://api.web3forms.com/submit with access_key
3. Web3Forms delivers email to tonyalidu@gmail.com
4. On success → Frontend also POSTs to /api/contact (backend)
5. Backend saves to PostgreSQL contacts table
6. If DB offline → Backend still returns 201 (Web3Forms handled delivery)
7. User sees "TRANSMISSION_COMPLETE"

